ved, visible on its detail page and via keyword search), the /products tag filter still lists the same 35 hard-coded seed tags — no \\\"deep-cleaning\\\"/\\\"qatag-robotic\\\" chip exists, so the new tag cannot be selected. It still offers removed tags \\\"cleaning\\\"/\\\"cordless\\\", which now return 0 products. Tags added when creating a product (\\\"qatag-travel\\\", \\\"qatag-compact\\\") are likewise absent.\", \"evidence\": \"filters.tags item count = 35 before and after the edit; document.querySelector(\\\"[data-semtag-id='filters.tags.item.qatag-robotic']\\\") === null.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Aeropress Go\\\" with tags \\\"qatag-travel, coffee, qatag-compact\\\"; detail page lists all three tags and searching \\\"qatag-compact\\\" on /products returns exactly that product (1 product found).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dyson tags edited from \\\"vacuum, cordless, smart-home, cleaning\\\" to \\\"vacuum, smart-home, deep-cleaning, qatag-robotic\\\": detail page shows exactly the new set; search \\\"qatag-robotic\\\" returns 1 product (Dyson); tag-filter \\\"cleaning\\\" now returns 0 products.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Admin category is a single-choice select (Tech Gadgets/Home Goods/Fitness). Saved as Home Goods → product shows \\\"Home\\\" badge on /products card, appears under /category/home related list (\\\"More in Home\\\") and homepage Home Goods count rose 3→4.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category filter Tech → 3 products found (all Tech); Fitness → 3 products found (all Fitness); All = 9.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/products lists 9 products; each card shows category badge, price, name, brief review, rating, image (unsplash src + alt) and a Buy Now action (target=_blank).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Price-range filter applies wrong/stale boundary and has no maximum handle\", \"actual\": \"Sorting (Newest/Top Rated/Price asc/desc) and the min-rating filter work correctly. But with the price slider showing $600–$2495 and no other filter active, the grid still lists Theragun Pro $599 and Bowflex SelectTech 552 $549 (7 products found) while excluding $399/$199 — i.e. the effective cut-off is ~$500, one step behind the displayed value, and it never self-corrects. The range slider also renders only a \\\"Minimum\\\" thumb, so a maximum price cannot be set.\", \"evidence\": \"filters.price.min=$600, filters.price.max=$2495, products.count=\\\"7 products found\\\", items include $599 and $549\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all admin additions and edits are lost on page reload\", \"actual\": \"After reloading, /product/qa-aeropress-go-xl shows \\\"Product Not Found\\\" and the admin list is back to the 9 seeded products with Dyson's price reverted from the saved $729 to $749 (tags and featured flag also reverted). localStorage and sessionStorage are both empty, so state lives only in memory for the current page session.\", \"evidence\": \"Object.keys(localStorage)=[] ; admin list length 9 after reload vs 10 before; admin.products.item.3.price = \\\"$749\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 catalogue products show exactly one category badge (Tech ×4, Home ×3, Fitness ×3 = 9 = total count); admin form exposes category as a single-choice select restricted to Tech Gadgets / Home Goods / Fitness, and a created/edited product landed in exactly one category.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Results violate the active price-range criterion\", \"actual\": \"Search, category and multi-tag criteria are respected (tags OR-combined: wireless+coffee → Sony + Breville; category tech → only Tech items; \\\"cleaning\\\" after tag removal → 0). But with the price filter showing $600–$2495 and no other filter active, the grid still returned Theragun Pro $599 and Bowflex SelectTech 552 $549 (7 products found); after resetting the handle to $0 the grid showed only 5 of 9 products, i.e. the applied price bound lags one interaction behind the displayed value.\", \"evidence\": \"filters.price.min=$600 → items include $599/$549; filters.price.min=$0 → \\\"5 products found\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation only covers name/category/description; price, review, image, retailer link and specifications are unvalidated\", \"actual\": \"A product (\\\"QA Invalid Probe\\\") was created successfully (\\\"Product created successfully\\\") with price = -50, empty Image URL, empty Full Review, affiliate link = \\\"not-a-url\\\" (plain text field, no URL validation) and zero specification rows. Only an empty name/description triggers \\\"Please fill in all required fields\\\"; rating is the sole numeric field bounded (HTML min=0/max=5), price has no min attribute.\", \"evidence\": \"admin list gained item \\\"QA Invalid Probe\\\"; price input attrs {type:number, min:\\\"\\\", max:\\\"\\\"}; affiliate-link input type=text with no pattern.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/does-not-exist-123 → \\\"Product Not Found\\\" with browse CTA and no product data; /category/bogus → \\\"Category Not Found\\\" with no product listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category, sort, rating and price changes all re-rendered the grid and updated products.count in place with no navigation/reload (URL stayed /products).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking name link \\\"Dyson V15 Detect\\\" → /product/dyson-v15-detect; clicking the MacBook card image → /product/macbook-pro-14 with product.name = Apple MacBook Pro 14\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking product.buy opened a new tab at https://example.com/dyson-v15 (the product's own retailer URL), rel=noopener noreferrer, target=_blank; grid Buy Now buttons carry the same per-product hrefs.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching filter from Tech to Fitness updated trigger label to \\\"Fitness\\\" and swapped displayed products/count instantly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/dyson-v15-detect shows name, category badge \\\"Home\\\", rating 4.7, price $749, brief description, 4 tags, 5 key specifications, full review, image (unsplash, alt=name) and Buy Now → https://example.com/dyson-v15.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dyson (Home): vacuum/cordless/smart-home/cleaning; Peloton (Fitness): cardio/cycling/smart-equipment/subscription; tag filter vocabulary on /products matches these and category/price/rating identical between card and detail views.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dyson V15 Detect: home featured card $749; /products card Home/$749/4.7/brief; /category/home card identical; detail page same name, category Home, $749, 4.7, same brief plus full 424-char review and 5 specs rendered without clamping (scrollHeight==clientHeight, no line-clamp).\"}]}"
